WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
John, Chapter Nine.

2
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.867
And as Jesus passed by, he saw a man which was blind from his birth.

3
00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:11.867
And his disciples asked him, saying, Master, who did sin, this man, or his parents, that he was born blind?

4
00:00:11.867 --> 00:00:19.333
Jesus answered, Neither hath this man sinned, nor his parents: but that the works of God should be made manifest in him.

5
00:00:19.333 --> 00:00:25.067
I must work the works of him that sent me, while it is day: the night cometh, when no man can work.

6
00:00:25.067 --> 00:00:28.400
As long as I am in the world, I am the light of the world.

7
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:46.800
When he had thus spoken, he spat on the ground, and made clay of the spittle, and he anointed the eyes of the blind man with the clay, And said unto him, Go, wash in the pool of Siloam, (which is by interpretation, Sent.) He went his way therefore, and washed, and came seeing.

8
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:53.733
The neighbours therefore, and they which before had seen him that he was blind, said, Is not this he that sat and begged?

9
00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:59.600
Some said, This is he: others said, He is like him: but he said, I am he.

10
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.200
Therefore said they unto him, How were thine eyes opened?

11
00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:14.267
He answered and said, A man that is called Jesus made clay, and anointed mine eyes, and said unto me, Go to the pool of Siloam, and wash: and I went and washed, and I received sight.

12
00:01:14.267 --> 00:01:17.867
Then said they unto him, Where is he?

13
00:01:17.867 --> 00:01:19.467
He said, I know not.

14
00:01:19.467 --> 00:01:22.933
They brought to the Pharisees him that aforetime was blind.

15
00:01:22.933 --> 00:01:27.600
And it was the sabbath day when Jesus made the clay, and opened his eyes.

16
00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:31.467
Then again the Pharisees also asked him how he had received his sight.

17
00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:37.200
He said unto them, He put clay upon mine eyes, and I washed, and do see.

18
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:43.867
Therefore said some of the Pharisees, This man is not of God, because he keepeth not the sabbath day.

19
00:01:43.867 --> 00:01:47.467
Others said, How can a man that is a sinner do such miracles?

20
00:01:47.467 --> 00:01:49.333
And there was a division among them.

21
00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:54.133
They say unto the blind man again, What sayest thou of him, that he hath opened thine eyes?

22
00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:56.933
He said, He is a prophet.

23
00:01:56.933 --> 00:02:06.267
But the Jews did not believe concerning him, that he had been blind, and received his sight, until they called the parents of him that had received his sight.

24
00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:10.933
And they asked them, saying, Is this your son, who ye say was born blind?

25
00:02:10.933 --> 00:02:12.933
how then doth he now see?

26
00:02:12.933 --> 00:02:28.400
His parents answered them and said, We know that this is our son, and that he was born blind: But by what means he now seeth, we know not; or who hath opened his eyes, we know not: he is of age; ask him: he shall speak for himself.

27
00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:38.533
These words spake his parents, because they feared the Jews: for the Jews had agreed already, that if any man did confess that he was Christ, he should be put out of the synagogue.

28
00:02:38.533 --> 00:02:41.733
Therefore said his parents, He is of age; ask him.

29
00:02:41.733 --> 00:02:48.667
Then again called they the man that was blind, and said unto him, Give God the praise: we know that this man is a sinner.

30
00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:57.867
He answered and said, Whether he be a sinner or no, I know not: one thing I know, that, whereas I was blind, now I see.

31
00:02:57.867 --> 00:03:01.600
Then said they to him again, What did he to thee?

32
00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.333
how opened he thine eyes?

33
00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:08.533
He answered them, I have told you already, and ye did not hear: wherefore would ye hear it again?

34
00:03:08.533 --> 00:03:10.533
will ye also be his disciples?

35
00:03:10.533 --> 00:03:16.533
Then they reviled him, and said, Thou art his disciple; but we are Moses' disciples.

36
00:03:16.533 --> 00:03:22.133
We know that God spake unto Moses: as for this fellow, we know not from whence he is.

37
00:03:22.133 --> 00:03:30.933
The man answered and said unto them, Why herein is a marvellous thing, that ye know not from whence he is, and yet he hath opened mine eyes.

38
00:03:30.933 --> 00:03:39.067
Now we know that God heareth not sinners: but if any man be a worshipper of God, and doeth his will, him he heareth.

39
00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:44.267
Since the world began was it not heard that any man opened the eyes of one that was born blind.

40
00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:47.200
If this man were not of God, he could do nothing.

41
00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:52.667
They answered and said unto him, Thou wast altogether born in sins, and dost thou teach us?

42
00:03:52.667 --> 00:03:54.267
And they cast him out.

43
00:03:54.267 --> 00:04:01.333
Jesus heard that they had cast him out; and when he had found him, he said unto him, Dost thou believe on the Son of God?

44
00:04:01.333 --> 00:04:05.867
He answered and said, Who is he, Lord, that I might believe on him?

45
00:04:05.867 --> 00:04:11.200
And Jesus said unto him, Thou hast both seen him, and it is he that talketh with thee.

46
00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.333
And he said, Lord, I believe.

47
00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:15.067
And he worshipped him.

48
00:04:15.067 --> 00:04:23.600
And Jesus said, For judgment I am come into this world, that they which see not might see; and that they which see might be made blind.

49
00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:29.733
And some of the Pharisees which were with him heard these words, and said unto him, Are we blind also?

50
00:04:29.733 --> 00:04:39.200
Jesus said unto them, If ye were blind, ye should have no sin: but now ye say, We see; therefore your sin remaineth.

